# Append-only ledgers with an id per row: a union merge keeps the rows both
# sides added at one place. It also keeps both versions of a row two sides
# edited, and revives a row one side deleted; the borrowck lane fails a
# duplicate id, and each path here must be in its LEDGERS.
examples/conformance/INDEX.md merge=union
compiler/tests/borrowck/CONFORMANCE.md merge=union
compiler/tests/drops/conformance.tsv merge=union

# A derived file, the measurement of the tree it ships with: it is never merged
# by hand. A rebase takes main's version whole, and `corpusdiff.py run
# --baseline` regenerates it. keep-main keeps %A, which is main's side on a
# rebase, on a cherry-pick onto main and in `git apply --3way`; `git merge
# main` into a branch keeps the branch's. The driver is defined in each clone's
# config by tools/git_setup.sh; without it git merges the text.
compiler/tests/corpusdiff/corpus_diff.tsv merge=keep-main
